{"archetypes":[{"name":"ledger-env-parity","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan adds RESEARCH_TMPDIR resolver keys and mandates env stripping in both Python subprocess env= and bash env -u blocks; verify key lists, precedence, and tmpdir binding match tokens.py resolver loops and cannot leak parent ledgers.","prompt_body":"Compare the planned env-var unset lists and tmpdir bindings in python/checks.py against the documented bash ingestion commands in skills/research/references/research-phase.md and the current resolve_session_id / resolve_token_ledger_path loops in python/tokens.py. Flag any missing keys, wrong precedence versus IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR and DESIGN_TMPDIR, or paths where stale LARCH_TOKEN_LEDGER or LARCH_TOKEN_SESSION_ID could still route sidecars to a parent ledger. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"research-collector-contract","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Research ingestion is prompt-only prose mapping COLLECT_ARGS indices to arch/edge/ext/sec slots with REVIEWER_FILE and retry-derived paths; verify that contract against collect-agent-results.sh output and research-phase.md section ordering.","prompt_body":"Check whether the planned research-phase ingestion block correctly maps COLLECT_ARGS order to arch, edge, ext, and sec slots, parses REVIEWER_FILE from collector output, and derives retry and ns-retry sidecar paths that actually exist in scripts/collect-agent-results.sh. Verify the proposed insertion point sits after collector parsing but before runtime-timeout fallback handling without skipping lanes whose STATUS is not OK. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sidecar-dual-ingestion","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Seven items hinge on pairing token append-record NDJSON writes with record-vendor-sidecar active-ledger ingestion across drafter, lint-fix, and research paths without duplicate legacy record-vendor calls.","prompt_body":"Trace each planned ingestion site in scripts/launch-codex-drafter.sh, python/checks.py _run_codex, and the new research-phase prose against python/cli.py token subcommands and current _run_codex behavior. Hunt gaps where NDJSON append would run without matching active-ledger ingestion, ingestion still gates on LAUNCHER_EXIT=0, duplicate record-vendor commands could fire for one sidecar, or --tmpdir targets the lane run_dir instead of the session implementation or research root. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
